{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1552778058,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0MjE4NjI1ODM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3232","origin":"github"},"title":"datalad add subds  adds files within subds to subds","message":"Relates to #3230, but filed separately since might be obsolete with the revolution's \"save does it all\" semantic, which if I got it right would replace `add` altogether.\n```\n(git-annex)hopa:/tmp/superds[master]git-annex\n$\u003e datalad create subds1; cd subds1; touch 123; cd ..; datalad add subds1\n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/superds/subds1 \ncreate(ok): /tmp/superds/subds1 (dataset)\n123@  dir/  subdir/  subds1/\nadd(ok): /tmp/superds/subds1/123 (file)\nadd(ok): /tmp/superds/subds1 (dataset)\nsave(ok): /tmp/superds/subds1 (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 2)\n  save (ok: 1)\n```\nso even though current dataset is superds, and IMHO most logical effect would be just adding `subds`   to `superds` (even without `-d`) we instead disregard that we are not under `subds` and perform recursive addition within it.","files":null}]}